==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|gelatine}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*gel-}}
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|gélatine||jelly, gel}}, from {{der|en|it|gelatina||jelly, gel}}, from {{m|it|gelare||to freeze}}, from {{der|en|la|gelō||to freeze}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈd͡ʒɛlətɪn/|/ˈd͡ʒɛlətiːn/|q2=less often}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-gelatin.ogg|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# A [[protein]] derived through partial [[hydrolysis]] of the [[collagen]] extracted from [[animal]] [[skin]], [[bone]]s, [[cartilage]], [[ligament]]s, etc.
# An [[edible]] [[jelly]] made from this material.
# A thin, [[translucent]] [[membrane]] used as a [[filter]] for photography or for [[theatrical]] [[lighting]] [[effect]]s.
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2010 |month=April |author=Frank Zullo |title=Imaging Prehistoric Sunrises |volume=38 |issue=4 |page=50 |magazine=Astronomy
|passage=For both images I placed a Kodak 4.0 neutral-density '''gelatin''' filter over the lens to reduce the Sun's brightness.}}

====Synonyms====
